---
layout: layouts/product.njk
permalink: /phone/applications/desktop/linux/
title: "VoiceTel Phone for Linux — Install Guide & FAQ"
description: "Download, install, and troubleshoot VoiceTel Phone and VoiceML Phone on Linux: AppImage, .deb, .rpm, Snap, or Flatpak, for x86-64 and arm64. SHA-256 checksums and FAQ."
platform: linux
---
{%- from "partials/v2/macros.njk" import arrow %}
{%- set voicetel = phoneApps.apps | where("key", "voicetel") | first %}
{%- set appImage = voicetel.desktop | where("platform", "linux") | where("format", "AppImage") | where("arch", "x86-64") | first %}

<section class="hero hero--page" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
	<div class="hero__bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
	<div class="container hero__inner">
		<div class="hero__copy">
			<p class="eyebrow">Desktop &middot; Linux</p>
			<h1 id="hero-heading">VoiceTel Phone for Linux.</h1>
			<p class="lede">Download, install, and troubleshoot the Linux app: AppImage, .deb, .rpm, Snap, or Flatpak, on x86-64 and arm64. VoiceML Phone, the same softphone for VoiceML accounts, is listed alongside.</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="#download">Download for Linux {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/phone/applications/desktop/">All desktop clients</a>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="hero__visual">
			{%- set kpis = [
				{ label: "Version", value: voicetel.version, sub: "Built " ~ voicetel.built },
				{ label: "AppImage", value: appImage.size, sub: "x86-64 · portable, no install" },
				{ label: "Packages", value: "5", suffix: "formats", sub: "AppImage · .deb · .rpm · Snap · Flatpak" },
				{ label: "Architectures", value: "x86-64", suffix: "+ arm64", sub: "arm64 builds for Raspberry Pi 4/5 and ARM servers" }
			] %}
			{% include "partials/v2/kpi-grid.njk" %}
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="download" aria-labelledby="download-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="section__head">
			<p class="eyebrow">1 &middot; Download</p>
			<h2 id="download-heading">Pick the package that matches your distro and CPU.</h2>
			<p class="lede"><strong>x86-64 / amd64</strong> for Intel and AMD, <strong>arm64</strong> for 64-bit ARM such as Raspberry Pi 4/5 and ARM servers. If you're unsure, use the <strong>AppImage</strong>: portable, no install. The .deb is for Debian / Ubuntu, the .rpm for Fedora / RHEL / openSUSE, and Snap and Flatpak (freedesktop 24.08) are universal.</p>
		</div>
		{%- for app in phoneApps.apps %}
		{%- set files = app.desktop | where("platform", platform) %}
		<h3 class="subsection-heading" id="download-{{ app.key }}">{{ app.name }} {{ app.version }}</h3>
		<div class="prose"><p>{{ app.audience }}</p></div>
		<div class="table-container">
			<table class="data-table">
				<thead>
					<tr><th scope="col">Build</th><th scope="col">SHA-256</th></tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					{%- for file in files %}
					<tr>
						<td>{{ file.format }} &middot; {{ file.arch }}<br><a href="{{ phoneApps.baseUrl }}{{ file.file }}">{{ file.file }}</a> &middot; {{ file.size }}</td>
						<td><code class="mono">{{ file.sha256 | replace(r/^(.{32})/, "$1<wbr>") | safe }}</code></td>
					</tr>
					{%- endfor %}
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		{%- endfor %}
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--white" id="verify" aria-labelledby="verify-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">2 &middot; Verify checksum</p>
				<h2 id="verify-heading">Compare the SHA-256 before you install.</h2>
				<p class="lede">Optional: validate file integrity by comparing SHA-256 checksums with <code>sha256sum</code> in your terminal.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual">
				{%- set steps = [
					{ title: "Open your terminal", body: "Run the commands from the directory where you saved the download." },
					{ title: "Run sha256sum", body: "<code>sha256sum VoiceTel-" ~ voicetel.version ~ ".AppImage</code>, or whichever file you downloaded." },
					{ title: "Compare the output", body: "It must match the value listed above for that file." }
				] %}
				{% include "partials/v2/step-list.njk" %}
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row row--reverse">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">3 &middot; Install</p>
				<h2 id="install-heading">One command per package format.</h2>
				<p class="lede">Commands use the VoiceTel Phone x86-64 file names; substitute the file you downloaded (for example <code>-arm64</code> or <code>VoiceML-</code>). Open your terminal in the download directory first.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual">
				{%- set code %}{% highlight "bash" %}# AppImage: make it executable, then double-click to launch.
# GUI alternative: right-click → Properties → Permissions →
# Allow executing file as program. Optional: ~/Applications
chmod +x VoiceTel-{{ voicetel.version }}.AppImage

# Debian / Ubuntu
sudo apt install ./VoiceTel-{{ voicetel.version }}.deb

# Fedora / RHEL / openSUSE
sudo dnf install ./VoiceTel-{{ voicetel.version }}.rpm

# Snap
sudo snap install --dangerous ./VoiceTel-{{ voicetel.version }}.snap

# Flatpak (freedesktop 24.08)
flatpak install ./VoiceTel-{{ voicetel.version }}.flatpak{% endhighlight %}{% endset %}
				{%- set terminal = { label: "Terminal", pill: "install", code: code } %}
				{% include "partials/v2/terminal.njk" %}
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--white" id="firstlaunch" aria-labelledby="firstlaunch-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">4 &middot; First launch</p>
				<h2 id="firstlaunch-heading">Start the app, allow the microphone, sign in.</h2>
				<p class="lede">VoiceTel Phone takes the SIP credentials provisioned in the customer portal; VoiceML Phone takes a VoiceML activation code instead.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual">
				{%- set steps = [
					{ title: "Start the app", body: "Start <strong>VoiceTel</strong> (or <strong>VoiceML</strong>) from your app launcher." },
					{ title: "Allow microphone access", body: "Allow access if your desktop environment prompts for it." },
					{ title: "Sign in", body: "Enter your VoiceTel SIP credentials (username, password, display name) as provisioned in the customer portal. In VoiceML Phone, enter your VoiceML activation code under <em>Settings &rarr; Auto Provision</em> instead." }
				] %}
				{% include "partials/v2/step-list.njk" %}
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="section__head">
			<p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
			<h2 id="faq-heading">Questions about VoiceTel Phone on Linux.</h2>
		</div>
		{%- set faqs = [
			{ q: "How do I uninstall?", a: "<strong>AppImage:</strong> delete the file. <strong>Debian / Ubuntu:</strong> <code>sudo apt remove voicetel-phone</code>. <strong>Fedora / Red Hat:</strong> <code>sudo rpm -e voicetel-phone</code>." },
			{ q: "No audio device or PipeWire issues", a: "Verify PulseAudio or PipeWire is running and select the correct input/output device in your system sound settings." },
			{ q: "Wayland screen sharing", a: "Install <code>xdg-desktop-portal</code> and your desktop-environment-specific portal (e.g. <code>xdg-desktop-portal-gnome</code> or <code>-kde</code>)." },
			{ q: "Pre-seed configuration", a: "User: <code>~/.config/VoiceTelPhone/voicetel.json</code> &middot; System-wide: <code>/etc/VoiceTelPhone/voicetel.json</code>." },
			{ q: "Upgrading from an earlier version?", a: "Fully quit the running app from the system tray (right-click &rarr; <em>Quit</em>) before installing; otherwise the single-instance lock re-focuses the old version." }
		] %}
		{% include "partials/v2/faq.njk" %}

		<div class="cta-band">
			<div class="cta-band__text">
				<h3 class="cta-band__title">Need credentials first?</h3>
				<p class="cta-band__body">Sign up to provision SIP credentials, then install VoiceTel Phone on every Linux workstation that needs to make calls.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="cta-band__actions cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary" href="/signup/">Sign up {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/phone/applications/desktop/">All desktop clients</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
